From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Subject: [PATCH] fprintd: report a lockout and send pam_fprintd to the password

libfprint reports FP_DEVICE_ERROR_LOCKED_OUT when a reader refuses to match
after too many failed attempts until the user authenticates another way.
fprintd reported it as verify-unknown-error, and pam_fprintd gave up
without saying why.

Report it as verify-lockout. pam_fprintd tells the user that there were too
many failed fingerprint attempts and to use the password, and returns
PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL at once, so the stack goes straight to the password,
which is also what ends the lockout.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
diff --git a/pam/pam_fprintd.c b/pam/pam_fprintd.c
index 95c430c..f180385 100644
--- a/pam/pam_fprintd.c
+++ b/pam/pam_fprintd.c
@@ -622,6 +622,13 @@ do_verify (sd_bus      *bus,
             {
               return PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL;
             }
+          else if (str_equal (data->result, "verify-lockout"))
+            {
+              /* Retrying cannot help: go straight to the password, which is
+               * also what ends the lockout. */
+              send_err_msg (data->pamh, _("Too many failed fingerprint attempts. Use your password."));
+              return PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL;
+            }
           else
             {
               send_err_msg (data->pamh, _("An unknown error occurred"));
diff --git a/src/device.c b/src/device.c
index 757c30a..a7b380d 100644
--- a/src/device.c
+++ b/src/device.c
@@ -622,6 +622,8 @@ verify_result_to_name (gboolean match, GError *error)
         return "verify-disconnected";
       else if (g_error_matches (error, FP_DEVICE_ERROR, FP_DEVICE_ERROR_TOO_HOT))
         return "verify-disconnected";
+      else if (g_error_matches (error, FP_DEVICE_ERROR, FP_DEVICE_ERROR_LOCKED_OUT))
+        return "verify-lockout";
       else if (g_error_matches (error, G_IO_ERROR, G_IO_ERROR_CANCELLED) ||
                g_error_matches (error, FP_DEVICE_ERROR, FP_DEVICE_ERROR_DATA_NOT_FOUND))
         return "verify-no-match";
diff --git a/src/net.reactivated.Fprint.Device.xml b/src/net.reactivated.Fprint.Device.xml
index 809ab53..e9c4843 100644
--- a/src/net.reactivated.Fprint.Device.xml
+++ b/src/net.reactivated.Fprint.Device.xml
@@ -193,6 +193,12 @@
 							The device was disconnected during the verification, no other actions should be taken, and you shouldn't use the device any more.
 						</doc:definition>
 					</doc:item>
+					<doc:item>
+						<doc:term>verify-lockout</doc:term>
+						<doc:definition>
+							The device refuses to match after too many failed attempts. It keeps refusing until the user authenticates another way, such as with their password, so the user should be asked for that instead. The verification is over.
+						</doc:definition>
+					</doc:item>
 					<doc:item>
 						<doc:term>verify-unknown-error</doc:term>
 						<doc:definition>
